(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-syntax/tests/asl/layoutCorpusLib.asl#" :text "Shared corpus lowering parity checks for A3 layout.asl vs the a/parse indentParser reference, used by sharded corpus test suites")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-syntax/tests/asl/layoutCorpusLib.asl#isParenOrInvalidFile" :text "old-syntax, fixture and deliberately-invalid files are not indented ASL and are outside this corpus entirely; the 10 generated float oracle files (~10k lines, one flat do-block each), the 2 generated depth-stress files (1e5-deep nested parens on a handful of lines) and the 192KB blog posts.asl (146s for one file alone) make per-file lowering and rendering cost pathological, so they are excluded on performance grounds rather than swept; SkyLoomVisualizer.asl, EngineeringBlog.asl, InBrowserAgent.asl and BlogView.asl make a/parse's tokenizer panic outright (ERR_PARSE: stringToFloat64) on numeric-looking text inside a string, which a Result match cannot catch, so they must be skipped before calling a/parse at all; confirmed by an exhaustive ip-only sweep of every other candidate file, which found no further panics")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-syntax/tests/asl/layoutCorpusLib.asl#knownMisparseReason" :text "known cases where a/parse itself silently misparses (returns ok with a corrupted tree) rather than erroring; confirmed by reading the source against the lay output, which matches the source and the ip output, which does not")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-syntax/tests/asl/layoutCorpusLib.asl#allCorpusFiles!" :text "the full, filtered, sorted corpus of indented tracked .asl files shared by every shard")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-syntax/tests/asl/layoutCorpusLib.asl#shardFiles" :text "shard k (1-based) covers files whose 0-based index in the sorted list satisfies index mod n == k-1")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-syntax/tests/asl/layoutCorpusLib.asl#expectedShardCount" :text "expected file count for shard k of n, independent of shardFiles, used to assert the partition is exact")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-syntax/tests/asl/layoutCorpusLib.asl#verifyUncached!" :text "single per-file check: dynamic exclusion when a/parse rejects the file outright, static exclusion for known non-erroring a/parse misparses, otherwise a real parity assertion")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-syntax/tests/asl/layoutCorpusLib.asl#verifyCached" :text "a proven cached pass replaces the parity check")
